# [The Ash Warren](ash_relic_doc)

**A dry hole - and the mission needs you to fly it anyway.**

There is no beacon piece here. Whoever scattered the Beacon stopped in this warren on the
way to somewhere else, and what they left behind is a record of where they went next. The
Cipher cannot be found without it.

That is the whole argument for a ruin with nothing in it: not every dig is a find, and a
campaign where every ruin holds treasure is a campaign where ruins stop meaning anything.
The payoff here is knowledge, and one very good piece of salvage for the trouble.

**All chambers, no boxes.** Nobody built this. It was bored out of a rock by something that
wanted to be underground, and then it was abandoned in a hurry - which is why half of it
has come down.

